    "narrative": "With limited options available on a light schedule, **Geraldo Perdomo** stands as our highest-ranked start at 55.17. While he lacks the ceiling of our typical sluggers, he benefits from a favorable matchup against Phillips, whose 4.33 xERA offers the most exploitable path to production on today's slate. **Taylor Ward** trails closely at 52.92; despite a tougher draw against Woo, **Taylor Ward** receives a significant +16% park adjustment that keeps him firmly in our starting mix. His leadoff positioning remains a vital stabilizer for our counting stats, even as the raw SP skill marks represent a slight drag on his efficiency.\n\nThe lower tier of our lineup, anchored by **Masyn Winn** (49.02) and **Gleyber Torres** (48.56), reflects the current volatility of our active bench. **Masyn Winn** narrowly edged out internal options due to his stable position in the order and a slight advantage in neutral park factors compared to the rest of the group. **Gleyber Torres** continues to struggle with a significant -13% penalty due to his dynamic platoon split against right-handed pitching; he remains a marginal play today, kept in the lineup only because our primary alternatives, including **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Will Smith**, are either off the schedule or currently sidelined on the IL. \n\nWe are monitoring the lack of elite speed in today\u2019s active lineup as a clear risk for our stolen base totals. With **Lawrence Butler**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Jung Hoo Lee** all inactive today, we lack the aggressive base-stealing profiles that usually define LawDog's competitive advantage. We are effectively playing for efficiency and AVG today, as no player in the starting group projects as a high-probability SB threat against today\u2019s battery matchups. We will continue to watch for late lineup adjustments for **Bryson Stott**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert** to ensure we aren't leaving production on the table should injuries or rest days shift the landscape before first pitch.",
